  "narrative": "All newly delivered discovery estimates fail the acceptance bar for a clinically meaningful association. With direction -1, a positive signed estimate corresponds to stronger dependency in the exposed group, but none of the intervals excludes zero in the hypothesized direction, and none has a signed point estimate clearly at or above the approximate 10% absolute scale. The closest case is H23: outcome_012 feature_020=1 versus 0 has signed estimate +0.0205 [-0.0007, 0.0418]. That point is only about 8.3% of the absolute mean for outcome_012, below the approximately 0.025 threshold, and its lower bound includes zero. Moreover, the same exposure on outcome_003 (H54) is essentially null and opposite-signed, so there is no cross-outcome coherence. Given that these 12 discovery tests used unadjusted 95% intervals and are not independent in outcome space, chasing H23 without a validation-quality signal would be vulnerable to multiplicity and split-level instability. H49 is also near the magnitude threshold in the opposite signed direction, but it is highly imbalanced (110 exposed, 1890 comparator), interval-crossing, and lower powered, so it does not support a scientifically meaningful difference. The remaining results for feature_027, feature_052, feature_021, feature_011, feature_023, and the rest of the screen are small, interval-crossing, or directionally inconsistent. No leakage, coding, or eligibility problem is apparent: all cells met the minimum sample-size requirement, nominal categorical levels were not treated as ordered, and unique/constant predictors were avoided. No independent validation is requested because none of these candidates reaches the evidence strength appropriate for validation; validation is better reserved for a comparison with an interval excluding zero and a point estimate at or beyond the clinical scale, preferably with some coherence.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted claims: none. Closed this iteration: feature_027, feature_052, feature_021, feature_020, and feature_011 screens on outcome_012 (H19-H21, H23-H24) and outcome_003 (H51-H55); outcome_015 feature_023 and feature_032 (H48-H49). H23 was the only borderline discovery estimate but was closed because the point estimate is below the approximate 10% threshold, the interval crosses zero, and outcome_003 coherence for feature_020 is absent. No validation was requested because no new result had sufficient strength to justify a validation comparison. Active untested registered claims remain: H27-H30, H33, H34, H36 on outcome_012; H56-H57 categorical contrasts on outcome_003; H58-H62 on outcome_005; H63-H64 on outcome_011. Next analysis should prioritize outcome_005 and outcome_011 marker screens and possibly new less-covered outcomes or continuous predictors, but avoid low-prevalence comparisons unless the effect is unambiguously large. All interpretations remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}

